  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Consider an infinite sequence XiX_iXi​ of nonnegative integers, in which X1=AX_1 = AX1​=A, X2=BX_2 = BX2​=B, X3=CX_3 = CX3​=C, and for i≥4i\\ge 4i≥4,\nXi=max⁡(Xi−3,Xi−2,Xi−1)−min⁡(Xi−3,Xi−2,Xi−1)X_i = \\max(X_{i-3}, X_{i-2}, X_{i-1}) - \\min(X_{i-3}, X_{i-2}, X_{i-1})Xi​=max(Xi−3​,Xi−2​,Xi−1​)−min(Xi−3​,Xi−2​,Xi−1​)\n\nFind the KKK-th term of this sequence.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe only line of each test case contains four space-separated integers A,B,C,KA, B, C, KA,B,C,K — the first three  terms of the sequence, and the index of the term that you have to find.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the KKK-th term of the corresponding sequence.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\le T \\le 10001≤T≤1000",
      "0≤A,B,C≤10180 \\le A, B, C \\le 10^{18}0≤A,B,C≤1018",
      "1≤K≤10181 \\le K \\le 10^{18}1≤K≤1018"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
